      ⍝
      ⍝ Regression (Blake McBride, LanguageVariances.md #13, 2026-08-10):
      ⍝ ⎕FC's default fill character for '8' positions used
      ⍝ UNI_STAR_OPERATOR (⋆, U+22C6, GNU APL's own canonical glyph for
      ⍝ the power primitive) instead of the ASCII asterisk (apl2lrm.txt
      ⍝ Figure 33 p.291 gives the default ⎕FC as `.,*0_¯`). Fixed to use
      ⍝ the already-existing UNI_ASTERISK constant (U+002A, tagged
      ⍝ F12_POWER same as UNI_STAR_OPERATOR -- both were already
      ⍝ recognized as alternate input glyphs for power, just the wrong
      ⍝ one was used as ⎕FC's default).
