      ⍝ regression (Blake McBride, Bugs12.md #6, 2026-08-06): an 'E' with
      ⍝ no digit position after it (directly, or via a pending exponent
      ⍝ flag reaching end-of-string / a right decorator before any digit
      ⍝ position) used to abort: Assertion failed:
      ⍝ row.size() == all_formats.size() in format_by_example()
      ⍝ (Bif_F12_FORMAT.cc:986), or -- with asserts off -- leave part of
      ⍝ the result's Cells uninitialized. Now rejected with DOMAIN ERROR.
      ⍝ '9.9E' (E as a plain right-decorator char, no pending exponent
      ⍝ flag) and '9E9' (E with a digit position) are unaffected.
