      ⍝ ⎕FC[5] print-as-blank (Blake McBride, LanguageVariances.md #14,
      ⍝ 2026-08-10) ----------------------------------
      ⍝
      ⍝ apl2lrm.txt p.141: ⎕FC[5] (default '_') marks a fixed separator
      ⍝ position within a picture's digit group -- it must not terminate
      ⍝ the digit group early (Bif_F12_FORMAT::is_control_char() didn't
      ⍝ recognize it at all, so the parser treated it as a trailing
      ⍝ decorator and truncated the digit group there) and must render
      ⍝ as a literal space without consuming a value digit.
      ⍝
      '555_555_5555'⍕8324632190
832 463 2190

      ⍝ print-as-blank in both the integer and fractional parts
      ⍝
      '55_55.55_55'⍕1234.5678
12 34.56 78

      ⍝ leading print-as-blank
      ⍝
      '_55555'⍕123
   123

      ⍝ regression for the fix's own self-referential trap: is_control_
      ⍝ char() is also used by Quad_FC::assign() to validate a *proposed*
      ⍝ ⎕FC[5] value (SystemVariable.cc) -- an earlier version of this
      ⍝ fix folded the ⎕FC[5] check directly into is_control_char(),
      ⍝ which made that validation self-referential: ⎕FC←'' (reset to
      ⍝ defaults) checked its own new '_' default against the *current*
      ⍝ ⎕FC[5] (already '_'), matched, and silently replaced it with a
      ⍝ space. Confirmed live before the fix (cross-testcase-file state:
      ⍝ ⎕FC[5] showed as space, not '_', partway through a full `make
      ⍝ test` run) and fixed by adding a separate is_picture_char() used
      ⍝ only by the picture parser, leaving is_control_char() untouched.
      ⍝
      ⎕FC←''
      ⎕FC
.,*0_¯

      '555_555_5555'⍕8324632190
832 463 2190

      ⍝ Regression: Bugs25 #3 (Blake McBride). A '0'/'9' zero-fill digit
      ⍝ combined with a ',' (or other non-digit decoration) in the same
      ⍝ sub-field always raised a bare DOMAIN ERROR -- Format_sub::
      ⍝ map_field() seeded/decremented min_len over *character* count
      ⍝ (including the comma) instead of *digit* count, so the field's
      ⍝ minimum digit requirement came out one too high and
      ⍝ insert_int_commas() ran out of digit slots. Fixed in
      ⍝ Bif_F12_FORMAT.cc by counting only Avec::is_digit() positions.
      ⍝
      '0,000'⍕1234
1,234

      '9,999'⍕1234
1,234

      '99,999'⍕1234
01,234

      '$9,999'⍕1234
$1,234

      '0,000.00'⍕1234.5
1,234.50

      ⍝ Regression: Bugs25 #3b, same root cause: fill_data_fields()'s
      ⍝ integer-part overflow check compared the digit count against
      ⍝ out_len (output *character* width, includes commas) instead of
      ⍝ the number of digit positions, so an overflowing value with a
      ⍝ comma in its picture slipped past the check and died later
      ⍝ inside insert_int_commas() with no )MORE explanation instead of
      ⍝ the proper "integer part exceeds A specification" message. Fixed
      ⍝ by comparing against the new Format_sub::digit_count instead.
      ⍝
      '5,555'⍕12345
DOMAIN ERROR+
      '5,555'⍕12345
      ^      ^
      )MORE
A⍕B : B does not fit into A (the integer part of 12345 has more digits than A)

      ⍝ Bugs28 #46: formatting a negative B through a picture with no
      ⍝ conditional ('1', '2', or '3') decorator is a DOMAIN ERROR, per
      ⍝ APL2 LRM p.141 ("'5' alone does not allow display of negative
      ⍝ values. Use 1 and 2 to control the display of signed numbers").
      ⍝
      ⍝ A sign decorator ('¯' or '-') without such a digit is a simple
      ⍝ decorator that is always displayed (LRM p.140). SVN 3711 had made
      ⍝ it float only-if-negative, which dropped the '-' after a field-
      ⍝ ending '6' in date patterns (reported by Christian Robert).
      ⍝
      '¯5.5'⍕1.5
¯1.5



      '-5.5'⍕1.5
-1.5



      '⊂5.5⊃'⍕1.5
⊂1.5⊃



      '0006-06-06 @ 06:06:06'⍕2026 10 12 5 40 47
2026-10-12 @ 05:40:47



      '0006/06/06 06:06'⍕1991 12 17 12 35
1991/12/17 12:35



      '55.55'⍕¯1.5
DOMAIN ERROR+
      '55.55'⍕¯1.5
      ^      ^
      )MORE
A⍕B : B does not fit into A (B is negative, but A has no conditional ('1', '2', or '3') non-blank decorator to show that, APL2 LRM p.141)

      )SIC



      '-5.5'⍕¯1.5
DOMAIN ERROR+
      '-5.5'⍕¯1.5
      ^     ^
      )MORE
A⍕B : B does not fit into A (B is negative, but A has no conditional ('1', '2', or '3') non-blank decorator to show that, APL2 LRM p.141)

      )SIC



      ⍝ the sign decorator floats only-if-negative with an explicit '1'
